  "body": "Deleting a comment could leave keyboard focus on the document body after its card disappeared. A retained parent could also lose focus while its confirmation dialog closed, including in WebKit. Return focus to the retained comment after dialog exit, or to that discussion\u2019s toggle if the card is removed; cancellation returns to the comment menu.\n\nAdds rendered regressions and real-API keyboard journeys for cancellation, leaf deletion and parent deletion with retained replies. Also records the completed PR #470 production rollout, schema 159, native qualification, store submission status and remaining physical-device verification limits.\n\nValidation: all 2,293 web tests (235 suites) pass in hosted UI CI, including the 19 focused rendered tests; 10 actual-API journeys on Chromium desktop/phone/tablet, Firefox and WebKit; typecheck, scoped lint, production bundle build and catalog audit pass. The focus regressions failed before repair; the first timer-only attempt failed WebKit and was replaced with dialog-exit focus restoration.\n\nThis is a compatible web-only follow-up. Production backend remains `645f56fcc44f81609fbfd0e03d683b40376ce77a`; no schema or native artifact changes. After protected merge, the restored Cloudflare production branch deployment will publish the web repair, followed by a fresh owned production focus canary.\n\nCurrent revision: `4731a35742b4939236bc08f43c5ea2780820caee`. [Cloudflare preview](https://827ffd4f.tdf-app.pages.dev) deployed successfully. [Hosted CI](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/36710064995) passed, including the broader persona browser suite; universal interaction properties, social/event verification, catalog audit, repository checks, API contracts, migration planning, monitoring and safe-install checks pass. The initial documentation-fingerprint failure was corrected by regenerating only the two changed release-document hashes; its contract check and local inventory/evidence tests pass.\n\nAll checks are green on this revision. This revision subsequently received independent approval and merged; see production evidence below. Cloudflare account access has been restored, and automatic production deployments are confirmed enabled with no temporary release hooks remaining.\n\nProduction completion (1 October 2026): independent maintainer `tdfrecords` approved the exact head, and protected auto-merge produced `adafd0c3795462c5b094622302658e24837fd277`. Its tree equals the tested/approved tree. Cloudflare production deployment `fd960cb4-2568-4a2e-a1bf-c7bd952bc64c` succeeded; both canonical public hosts serve its identical entry bundle. Real production desktop, phone and WebKit flows passed keyboard cancellation, leaf deletion focus, retained parent focus/replies and axe without serious/critical violations. All owned canary bodies were deleted, the temporary source hidden and credentials revoked. The existing backend remains healthy at `645f56fcc44f81609fbfd0e03d683b40376ce77a`, schema 159, with no backend/native/schema changes for this repair.\n\nA post-merge audit detected a newly updated DOMPurify advisory in the existing lockfile; separate minimal dependency PR #474 fixes it without weakening the audit policy. That patch is now independently approved, merged and deployed as `49f1f0ec087067d17f62d91df1b616eb053eb894`. All post-merge checks pass, including the restored security audit. Final production desktop/phone/WebKit focus checks also pass; full evidence is recorded in PR #474.\n",
